  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Intransitive godan verb. Xが{治|おさ}まる. The transitive pair is {治|おさ}める (to govern; to bring under control).\n\nUsed of pain, fever, wind, anger, or social unrest growing calm.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {痛|いた}みが{治|おさ}まる: the pain subsides\n- {怒|いか}りが{治|おさ}まる: one's anger cools\n- {風雨|ふうう}が{治|おさ}まる: the wind and rain die down\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {収|おさ}まる: to fit in; to settle — used of things fitting a space, or a situation reaching a conclusion\n- {治|なお}る: to recover; to be cured — of an illness or injury being fully healed, not just calming",
